target
Cargo.lock
__pycache__

*.log
ok

# Compiled program output (jinnc default binary name)
a.out
**/a.out

# Store/WAL/index runtime artifacts produced by running programs and
# benchmarks. A store's path is its declared name relative to the process
# cwd, so any program with a `store` decl writes these wherever it is run
# from ( `<store>.store`, `<store>.wal`, `<store>.<field>.idx` ). Tests
# and benchmarks run their binaries inside a scratch cwd; use .data/ for
# ad-hoc runs so the repo root stays clean.
*.store
*.wal
*.idx
.data/*
!.data/README.md

# Benchmark run outputs. results.csv is deliberately TRACKED: it is the
# published baseline (with hardware/run-count header and per-row
# comparability tags) that ci/bench_regression.py gates against; regenerate
# and commit it only as a deliberate re-baselining. The JSON outputs are
# scratch.
benchmarks/_build/
benchmarks/results*.json

# Compiled demo/app binaries and packaged tarballs. `jinn build` and
# `jinn package` write these next to the sources; they are build outputs,
# not source, and shipping an ELF in the repo makes review harder.
apps/*/dist/
apps/alpha_release_demo/alpha_demo

.ryu
.ryu/**
